  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "In 2025 and 2026 statements, Erwin Gianchandani described AI as holding transformative potential to reshape how the world functions and as already reshaping how Americans work, learn, build, and create new technologies. He said NSF's AI-ready test beds program is designed to help academia and industry researchers accelerate that transformation by simulating real-world conditions AI systems will encounter as they scale and deploy. In 2024 and 2025 statements, he characterized NSF investments in AI-enabled protein design and programmable cloud laboratories as efforts to accelerate scientific progress, overcome adoption barriers, and maintain U.S. biotechnology leadership.",
   "sids": [
    "s2",
    "s6",
    "s7",
    "s1",
    "s3",
    "s4",
    "s8"
   ],
